# C++ Loop and Array

## Description

This program demonstrates the use of an array and a `for` loop in C++. It stores the marks of five students in an array and displays each mark using a loop.

## Variables Used

### 1. marks
An integer array that stores the marks of five students.

### 2. i
The loop variable used to access each array element.

## Main Function

The `main()` function initializes an array with five student marks. A `for` loop starts from index 0 and continues until index 4 to access and display every element of the array.

## Output

78 82 91 67 88

## Concept Used

- Arrays
- for Loop
- Array Indexing
- Iteration

## Program Flow

Start
  ↓
Create and Initialize Array
  ↓
Initialize i = 0
  ↓
Check i < 5
  ↓
Display marks[i]
  ↓
Increment i
  ↓
Repeat Until i = 5
  ↓
End